  "prompt_text": "The figure illustrates a compact optical waveguide device in side and top view, showing how a laser injects light into a patterned guiding structure and how that light is routed through the chip. In the side view, a laser beam enters from above near one end of a long, thin structure about 1.6 mm long and 15 µm thick. The light appears to couple into the primary waveguide through a sloped ramp, then travel horizontally as a photon along the guide. A small internal step or barrier is included in the path, and angled end features labeled as mirrors suggest that the light is confined or redirected within the structure.\n\nThe top view clarifies the layout of two coupled channels: a straight primary waveguide and a lower secondary waveguide. Light first propagates along the primary guide, then enters a region where the path oscillates sinusoidally into the secondary guide before returning toward the primary path. Overall, the figure conveys a fabricated photonic element designed to inject, guide, and manipulate light on a microscale using geometric features such as ramps, barriers, mirrors, and coupled waveguides.",
